\nportable. The numeric policies are deliberately hardware/model fits. The\nhighest-risk values to carry unchanged are split-K, CTA residency assumptions,\nthe four Llama projection shapes, fused N=128, and prefill N=1856.\n\n## 12. Recommended port-validation sequence\n\n1. Measure compression ratio and exception histograms for all target-model\n   layers and real KV blocks.\n2. Measure CPU weight/KV encode with the target ISA. Add AVX2/AVX-512 on x86\n   before judging the ARM-vectorized implementation.\n3. Verify bit-exact resident weight and KV decode, then measure it separately\n   from H2D.\n4. Measure H2D-only with the target CPU/GPU fabric and actual residency split.\n5. Profile registers, shared memory, spills, active CTAs, barrier stalls, and\n   tensor-pipe utilization for N=16/32/48/64/128.\n6. Re-sweep split-K for every production projection shape and tensor-parallel\n   configuration.\n7. Recalibrate fused/standalone and standalone/raw boundaries under concurrent\n   serving H2D.\n8. Only then run full TTFT/TPOT comparisons against P4Flat. Do not infer full\n   serving speedup by summing isolated microbenchmarks.\n\n## 13. Result and source locations\n\n- Consolidated implementation manifest:\n  `/lambda/nfs/whchoi/startup-patches/tiered-serve/CD3_CURRENT_MANIFEST.md`\n- Consolidated startup patch:\n  `/lambda/nfs/whchoi/startup-patches/tiered-serve/cd3_current.patch`\n- vLLM CD3 integration patch:\n  `/lambda/nfs/whchoi/startup-patches/tiered-serve/cd3_vllm_integration.patch`\n- Final fused comparison CSVs:\n  `/lambda/nfs/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260901-route/final-comparison/`\n- Standalone/raw prefill report:\n  `/lambda/nfs/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260901-route/PREFILL_ROUTE_REPORT.md`\n- Fused route/all-layer raw logs and CSVs:\n  `/lambda/nfs/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260901-route/`\n- Final standalone and 16-layer KV logs:\n  `/lambda/nfs/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260901-route/kv_standalone_final_20260901.log`\n  and `